SUMMARY:Home Away from Home: Student Life on Campus
DESCRIPTION:Spanning across four decades—1970s to the 2000s—items inc
 luding scrapbooks\, photographs\, student papers\, and handbooks demonstr
 ate life on and off campus. From decorating dorm rooms to chasing campus 
 ghosts\, students have always found ways to build community and make new 
 memories. This exhibit highlights the student experience and the multitud
 e of ways students found a sense of home\, identity and belonging at Indi
 ana University.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Spanning across four decades—1970s to
  the 2000s—items including scrapbooks\, photographs\, student papers\, 
 and handbooks demonstrate life on and off campus. From decorating dorm ro
 oms to chasing campus ghosts\, students have always found ways to build c
 ommunity and make new memories. This exhibit highlights the student exper
 ience and the multitude of ways students found a sense of home\, identity
  and belonging at Indiana University.</p>
