DTSTART:20260902T180000Z
DTEND:20260902T190000Z
SUMMARY:Introduction to Data Management Support at IU
DESCRIPTION:Attendees will learn best practices for research data managem
 ent\, including how to organize\, document\, and preserve their data effe
 ctively. The session will also highlight the specific tools\, resources\,
  and support services available at IU to help researchers succeed at ever
 y stage of their work.__________  New to research\, new to managing your 
 own data\, or interested in learning more about research data support at 
 IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 semester\, join us for webinars desi
 gned to walk you through the basics of researching with data at IU— fro
 m organizing and storing your data to meeting funder requirements and fin
 ding the right tools.  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Research Data Comm
 ons\, and other campus partners\, with sessions useful for researchers at
  any stage. Some sessions may require advanced registration.  For any que
 stions\, please contact the IU Libraries Research Data Services team (res
 data@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@iu.edu)) - and don't forget to check back reg
 ularly\, as new sessions are added!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-contrast="none">Attendees will
  learn best practices for research data management\, including how to org
 anize\, document\, and preserve their data effectively. The session will 
 also highlight the specific tools\, resources\, and support services avai
 lable at IU to help researchers succeed at every stage of their work.</sp
 an><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;134233117&quot\;:false\,&quot\;134233118
 &quot\;:false\,&quot\;335559738&quot\;:240\,&quot\;335559739&quot\;:0}"><
 /span></p><p><span data-contrast="none">__________</span></p><p>  New to 
 research\, new to managing your own data\, or interested in learning more
  about research data support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 seme
 ster\, join us for webinars designed to walk you through the basics of re
 searching with data at IU— from organizing and storing your data to mee
 ting funder requirements and finding the right tools.</p><p>  Hosted by I
 U Libraries\, the IU Research Data Commons\, and other campus partners\, 
 with sessions useful for researchers at any stage. Some sessions may requ
 ire advanced registration.</p><p>  For any questions\, please contact the
  IU Libraries Research Data Services team (<a href="mailto:resdata@iu.edu
 ">resdata@iu.edu</a>) - and don't forget to check back regularly\, as new
  sessions are added!</p>
