SUMMARY:Developing a Secure and Private Research Roadmap from Project Ide
 a to Data Destruction
DESCRIPTION:This session introduces SecureMyFutureResearch\, a course des
 igned to help graduate-level researchers anticipate these requirements be
 fore they create delays\, uncertainty\, or risks to research data. Partic
 ipants will receive an overview of the course's six-stage research lifecy
 cle roadmap\, from developing a project and obtaining approvals through d
 ata collection\, retention\, sharing\, and destruction.__________  New to
  research\, new to managing your own data\, or interested in learning mor
 e about research data support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 sem
 ester\, join us for webinars designed to walk you through the basics of r
 esearching with data at IU— from organizing and storing your data to me
 eting funder requirements and finding the right tools.  Hosted by IU Libr
 aries\, the IU Research Data Commons\, and other campus partners\, with s
 essions useful for researchers at any stage. Some sessions may require ad
 vanced registration.  For any questions\, please contact the IU Libraries
  Research Data Services team (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@iu.edu)) - a
 nd don't forget to check back regularly\, as new sessions are added!
